Authored arnold:global color spaces override renderingColorSpace with Hydra 2

The render settings prim of with_global.usda authors renderingColorSpace = "lin_b",
arnold:global:color_space_linear = "lin_a" and arnold:global:color_space_narrow = "lin_c". As in the
usd procedural, the arnold attributes must be used, so the color manager gets "lin_a" and "lin_c" in
every pass. Before the fix, the Hydra 2 render settings prim dropped the arnold:global color spaces as
unknown options, and "lin_b" was used. without_global.usda only authors renderingColorSpace, which
must then be used.

See ARNOLD-18814

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {}
